Package: hd-network
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-jinja2, systemd, hd-config
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian network configuration
 Renders the systemd-networkd files in /etc/systemd/network from the key
 hd-network in the hyprdebian configuration, /etc/hyprdebian/config.json:
 interfaces with DHCP or static addresses, bridges with a fixed MAC address
 and their ports, and whether the boot waits for the network.
 .
 hd-network-iface and hd-network-bridge add, change and remove interfaces
 and bridges in the settings, which they write with hd-config-update.
 hd-network-render writes the files and reloads systemd-networkd. The
 package also names ethernet and wifi interfaces by their path, such as
 enp3s0, with a persistent MAC address, also in the initramfs. Installing it
 configures nothing.
